#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.title"
msgid "The three pieces of paper"
msgstr "Los tres documentos"

#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.hook"
msgid ""
"Two documents decide whether you walk out with ID. One has a deadline near "
"release; the other is worth starting years out."
msgstr ""
"Dos documentos deciden si sales con identificación. Uno tiene una fecha "
"límite cerca de tu salida; el otro conviene empezarlo con años de "
"anticipación."

#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.0.title"
msgid "Everything runs through your ID"
msgstr "Todo pasa por tu identificación"

msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"A bank account, an apartment, a job, and every single thing you will ever do"
" with a credit bureau needs a photo ID. And the ID itself needs two other "
"documents first. Get this chain wrong and nothing downstream of it can "
"start."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.0.aside"
msgid ""
"If your date is years away, this lesson still has one thing in it for you: "
"the birth certificate. It has no deadline, it takes ten weeks or more, and "
"asking for it early costs you nothing. The rest of this course does not wait"
" for a release date at all."
msgstr ""
"Si tu fecha está a años de distancia, esta lección todavía tiene algo para "
"ti: el acta de nacimiento. No tiene fecha límite, tarda diez semanas o más, "
"y pedirla desde ya no te cuesta nada. El resto de este curso no depende de "
"una fecha de salida."

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.1.title"
msgid "Birth certificate and Social Security card, in that order of worry"
msgstr ""
"Acta de nacimiento y tarjeta del Seguro Social, en ese orden de preocupación"

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"Both have to be in your file before the non-driver ID application can even "
"be sent. Your coordinator is the one who requests them, and they check where"
" everyone's documents stand every three months. The birth certificate is the"
" slow one. It can take ten weeks or more to come back, so it is the one to "
"ask about first."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.2.title"
msgid "120 days out, ask for the Social Security card"
msgstr "A 120 días de salir, pide la tarjeta del Seguro Social"

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"That is the mark. At 120 days before you go home, the Social Security card "
"application goes in. If you are inside that window right now and nobody has "
"raised it with you, raise it with them. If you are years out, this is the "
"date to know about rather than the date to act on, and it will come round."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.2.aside"
msgid ""
"Write the date down. It is the one deadline in this whole course that is "
"yours to chase rather than somebody else's."
msgstr ""
"Anota la fecha. Es la única fecha límite de todo este curso que te toca a ti"
" perseguir y no a otra persona."

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.3.title"
msgid "The birth certificate is free, unless you were born somewhere else"
msgstr "El acta de nacimiento es gratis, salvo que hayas nacido en otro lugar"

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"When the department requests your birth certificate for your release, there "
"is no fee, and your sentence and commitment paperwork counts as your "
"permission, so you do not have to sign anything separately. That covers New "
"York records only. Born in another state, or another country, and none of "
"that applies to you. Say so early, because yours takes longer and costs "
"money."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.4.title"
msgid "The other 120 days, which is not the same 120 days"
msgstr "Los otros 120 días, que no son los mismos 120 días"

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.card.4.body"
msgid ""
"After you are released, the DOCCS ID you walk out with expires in 120 days. "
"That is your window to get to a DMV office and trade it for a real non-"
"driver photo ID. Two different 120-day clocks, one before the gate and one "
"after, and mixing them up is how people end up with no ID at all."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"You are 130 days from release and have no birth certificate on file. What is"
" the most useful thing to do?"
msgstr ""
"Estás a 130 días de salir y no tienes acta de nacimiento en tu expediente. "
"¿Qué es lo más útil que puedes hacer?"

msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.check.why"
msgid ""
"The birth certificate has no deadline attached, which is exactly why it gets"
" left. It is also the slow one, ten weeks or more, and the ID application "
"cannot be submitted without it. The 120-day mark is for the Social Security "
"card. The birth certificate wants to be moving before that."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.check.choice.both"
msgid "Ask your coordinator about both documents now"
msgstr "Preguntarle a tu coordinador por ambos documentos ahora"

#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.check.choice.wait"
msgid "Wait until 120 days, then ask about both"
msgstr "Esperar a los 120 días y luego preguntar por ambos"

#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lesson.three-papers.check.choice.id"
msgid "Apply for the photo ID and sort the rest later"
msgstr "Solicitar la identificación con foto y resolver lo demás después"

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.title"
msgid "What a credit report actually is"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.hook"
msgid ""
"It is a file about you that you have never read, and there are rules about "
"who gets to look at it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.0.title"
msgid "It is a list, not a judgement"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"A credit report is a record of accounts in your name: who you borrowed from,"
" how much, whether you paid on time, and whether anybody is chasing you for "
"it. That is it. It is closer to a bank statement than to a grade."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.1.title"
msgid "There are three of them, and they disagree"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"Equifax, Experian and TransUnion each keep their own file on you. Not every "
"lender reports to all three, so an account can sit on one report and be "
"missing from another. This is why anything we do, we do three times."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.2.title"
msgid "Not everybody can just look you up"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"A report can only be handed out for a reason the law lists: you applied for "
"credit, an insurer is making a decision, a court ordered it, child support "
"enforcement, or you told them in writing to release it. Somebody being "
"curious about you is not on that list."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.3.title"
msgid "An employer needs your written permission"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"An employer has to tell you clearly and in writing that they want to pull "
"your credit, and get your written permission before they do. If they then "
"decide not to hire you because of what is in it, they have to give you a "
"copy of the report and a written statement of your rights before they act. "
"Not after. Before."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.card.3.aside"
msgid ""
"This one matters on the outside. Most people never ask for the copy they are"
" owed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"An employer turns you down and mentions your credit. What are you owed?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.check.why"
msgid ""
"You get a copy of the report they used and a written statement of your "
"rights, and you are supposed to get it before they finalize the decision, so"
" there is a window to point out an error. Separately, a denial like this "
"entitles you to a free copy from the bureau itself. That comes up in the "
"lesson on free reports."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.check.choice.copy"
msgid "A copy of the report and a statement of your rights"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.check.choice.nothing"
msgid "Nothing, it is their decision"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-a-report-is.check.choice.reason"
msgid "A written explanation of their reasoning"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.title"
msgid "The report and the score are different things"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.hook"
msgid ""
"One is a file. The other is somebody's opinion about the file, and you are "
"owed the first one but not the second."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.card.0.title"
msgid "The file is the facts. The score is an opinion about them"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"The report lists what happened. A score is a number a company calculates "
"from that list, using a formula they own. Change the file and the score "
"follows. Argue with the score and nothing happens, because there is nothing "
"there to argue with."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.card.1.title"
msgid "Your free report may come with no number on it"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"What you are owed by law is the file. A score is specifically not part of "
"what they have to disclose. So when your report arrives in the mail and "
"there is no number anywhere on it, nothing has gone wrong and nobody has "
"cheated you. You got exactly what you were owed, and it is the more useful "
"half."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.card.2.title"
msgid "Your Social Security number can be blacked out"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"You can require them to leave the first five digits of your Social off your "
"own copy. That is a right you can insist on, not a favour. It is also the "
"reason you can read your own report on a tablet in a room full of people."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.check.prompt"
msgid "Your free report arrives and there is no score on it. What happened?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.check.why"
msgid ""
"The law says they owe you the file, and specifically says scores are not "
"part of that. Most mailed reports arrive without one. It says nothing about "
"whether you have a score, and the file is the part that can actually be "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.check.choice.normal"
msgid "Nothing. A file disclosure does not have to include one"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.check.choice.error"
msgid "They made a mistake and you should write back"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.report-and-score.check.choice.nofile"
msgid "It means you have no score at all"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.title"
msgid "There is no such thing as your credit score"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.hook"
msgid ""
"Not one number. Dozens, all real at the same time, and the free app on "
"somebody's phone is showing a different one from the bank."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.0.title"
msgid "Three things multiply together"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"Which bureau's file it was run against, which company's model did the "
"running, and what the score is for. Three bureaus, several models in active "
"use, and separate versions tuned for car loans and credit cards. Multiply "
"those out and one person honestly has dozens of scores on the same day."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.1.title"
msgid "They do not even share a scale"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"Most scores run 300 to 850. The ones car dealers and card companies pull run"
" 250 to 900. So a 700 in one place is not the same as a 700 in another, and "
"comparing them straight across tells you nothing."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.2.title"
msgid "Why the free app disagrees with the bank"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"Free apps usually show a VantageScore. Most lenders use a FICO. Different "
"companies, different formulas. Neither is lying to you. They are not "
"measuring the same thing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.3.title"
msgid "So which one is real?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"The one belonging to whoever is deciding about you. That is the whole "
"answer. A landlord, a car dealer and a card company will each pull a "
"different one, and all of them are real. Which is why the work is on the "
"file, not on chasing a number."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.card.3.aside"
msgid ""
"It is also why this app does not show you a number. A score with no model, "
"bureau and date attached is a guess that looks precise."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.check.prompt"
msgid "A free app shows 640. A car dealer says you are at 590. Who is wrong?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.check.why"
msgid ""
"The app is almost certainly showing a VantageScore. The dealer pulled an "
"auto-specific FICO, which runs on a 250 to 900 scale rather than 300 to 850,"
" probably from a different bureau's file. Both numbers can be correct at "
"once. Worth knowing before you assume somebody is running a game on you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.check.choice.neither"
msgid "Neither. Different model, different bureau, different scale"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.check.choice.app"
msgid "The app, those are never accurate"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.no-single-score.check.choice.dealer"
msgid "The dealer, they lowball to sell you a worse rate"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.title"
msgid "What actually moves a score"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.hook"
msgid "Five things, and two of them are most of it."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.card.0.title"
msgid "The five, by weight"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"Payment history is about 35 percent. How much you owe against what is "
"available to you is about 30 percent. How long you have had credit, about 15"
" percent. Your mix of types of credit, about 10 percent. Recently opened "
"accounts, about 10 percent."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.card.1.title"
msgid "Two of them are two thirds"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"Paying on time and not using too much of what you have available are roughly"
" 65 percent of it between them. Everything else is noise by comparison. If "
"you only ever remember one thing from this course, remember that the boring "
"answer is most of the answer."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.card.2.title"
msgid "The one nobody explains"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"That second one is about the ratio, not the amount. A card with a 500 dollar"
" limit carrying a 450 balance looks worse than a card with a 5,000 dollar "
"limit carrying the same 450. Same debt. Very different picture. Paying a "
"card down below about a third of its limit is the fastest legitimate move "
"there is."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.card.3.title"
msgid "Time is the one you cannot rush"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"Length of history only goes one way and only at one speed. Which is the real"
" argument for starting inside rather than at the gate: an account opened now"
" is already months old by the time anybody asks you for a credit check."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"You have 450 dollars and two cards, each with a 500 dollar limit and a 450 "
"balance. What helps your score most?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.check.why"
msgid ""
"Clearing one card takes it from 90 percent used to nearly nothing, which is "
"the part of the formula that moves fastest. Splitting it leaves both cards "
"around 45 percent used, which is better than 90 but not by as much. Keep "
"paying at least the minimum on the other one either way, because payment "
"history is the bigger slice and a missed payment undoes this."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.check.choice.one"
msgid "Pay one card down to near zero"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.check.choice.split"
msgid "Split it evenly across both"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.what-moves-it.check.choice.save"
msgid "Keep it in savings and pay the minimums"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.title"
msgid "Old debt does not last forever"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.hook"
msgid ""
"Most of it has to come off after seven years, and paying it does not restart"
" the clock."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.card.0.title"
msgid "Seven years, ten for bankruptcy"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"Collection accounts and charge-offs have to come off seven years after the "
"account first went delinquent. So do civil judgments and paid tax liens, and"
" most other bad marks. Bankruptcy runs ten. After that they are not allowed "
"to report it."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.card.1.title"
msgid "The clock starts at the original delinquency"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"This is the part that gets people. The seven years runs from when you first "
"fell behind on the original account, not from when a collector bought it and"
" not from when you paid it. Paying an old debt does not restart anything. A "
"collector who tells you it will is selling you something."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.card.2.title"
msgid "Court debt is a different animal"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"Restitution, fines and child support do not work like credit accounts. Civil"
" judgments largely came off credit reports back in 2017, and in New York "
"restitution is collected by probation rather than reported as a debt. Child "
"support arrears are the exception: states are required to report those. They"
" all matter, and they belong in a different list from your credit accounts."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"A collector says paying a five-year-old debt will help your credit. Is that "
"right?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.check.why"
msgid ""
"It may help, and on some newer scoring models a paid collection stops "
"counting against you entirely. But it does not restart or extend the seven "
"years, and it does not erase the entry. Anyone telling you that you have to "
"pay to make it go away has it backwards: time makes it go away. Get any "
"agreement in writing before money moves."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.check.choice.partly"
msgid "Partly, but it will not reset the seven years"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.check.choice.yes"
msgid "Yes, paying always helps"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.old-debt.check.choice.no"
msgid "No, never pay an old debt"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.title"
msgid "Every way to get your report free"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.hook"
msgid ""
"There are more routes than the one everybody knows, and coming home "
"qualifies you for several of them at once."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.0.title"
msgid "One a year, from all three, by mail"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"Every nationwide bureau owes you one free copy of your file every 12 months,"
" through one central request, and they have 15 days from getting the request"
" to send it. One letter to one address covers all three."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.1.title"
msgid "The mail route is the one that works from here"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"The Annual Credit Report Request Form goes to the Annual Credit Report "
"Request Service in Atlanta. No internet, no phone, no fee. The weekly free "
"reports everyone talks about are online only and are a voluntary arrangement"
" rather than a right, so they are no use to you in here."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.2.title"
msgid "Turned down for something? That is another free one"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"If you are denied credit, an apartment, insurance or a job because of your "
"credit report, you can get a free copy of the file they used, as long as you"
" ask within 60 days of being told. This is separate from your annual one and"
" does not use it up."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.3.title"
msgid "Unemployed or on assistance? Another one"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"A free report is also owed once a year to anyone who certifies in writing "
"that they are unemployed and planning to look for work in the next 60 days, "
"that they receive public assistance, or that they think their file has "
"errors from fraud. Somebody just home often qualifies under two or three of "
"those at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.card.3.aside"
msgid ""
"Almost nobody knows this one. It is worth remembering for the first year "
"out, when you will want to check more than once."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"You used your annual free report in March. In July a landlord turns you down"
" over your credit. Do you have to pay?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.check.why"
msgid ""
"Being turned down because of a report starts its own entitlement, separate "
"from the annual one, as long as you ask within 60 days. If you were also "
"unemployed or on assistance at the time, that is another separate route "
"again. These stack. Most people pay for something they were already owed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.check.choice.free"
msgid "No. A denial entitles you to another free copy"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.check.choice.pay"
msgid "Yes, you already used this year's"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.free-reports.check.choice.wait"
msgid "No, but you have to wait until next March"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.title"
msgid "What a dispute is, and the clock it starts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.hook"
msgid ""
"It is the one part of this where somebody else is on a deadline instead of "
"you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.0.title"
msgid "You are telling them their file is wrong"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"A dispute is a letter saying a specific item on your report is not accurate,"
" and why. Not a complaint, not a request for sympathy. One item, one reason,"
" in writing."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.1.title"
msgid "Thirty days, counted from when they get it"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"They have 30 days to investigate, starting the day the letter lands, not the"
" day you posted it. If you send more information during those 30 days they "
"get up to 15 more, so it can run to 45. Then they have five business days to"
" write and tell you the outcome."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.2.title"
msgid "Wrong, incomplete, or unprovable all count"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"If what they find is inaccurate, incomplete, or they simply cannot verify "
"it, they have to delete or fix it. That last one matters more than people "
"expect. An old debt sold on three times may have nobody left who can prove "
"it was ever yours."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.3.title"
msgid "All three, every time"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"An item deleted at Equifax is still sitting on the Experian and TransUnion "
"files. One letter fixes one third of the problem. This is why every dispute "
"here goes out as three letters."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.4.title"
msgid "It works more often than people think"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.disputes.card.4.body"
msgid ""
"In the FTC's study, about one in four people found at least one error on a "
"report that could have mattered, and about one in twenty had one bad enough "
"to cost them worse terms on a loan. One in five had an error put right after"
" they disputed it. Disputing is not a long shot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"You mail a dispute on the 1st. It arrives on the 5th. When is the answer "
"due?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.check.why"
msgid ""
"The clock runs from receipt, not from the postmark, which is why anything "
"sent from here should be tracked if possible. And if you send extra "
"paperwork while they are investigating, you hand them up to 15 extra days, "
"so send everything at once rather than in pieces."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.check.choice.receipt"
msgid "30 days from the 5th, when they received it"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.check.choice.posted"
msgid "30 days from the 1st, when you posted it"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.disputes.check.choice.either"
msgid "There is no fixed deadline"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.title"
msgid "Building a file from nothing"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.hook"
msgid ""
"No file is not the same as bad credit, and it is the faster of the two to "
"fix."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.0.title"
msgid "Empty moves faster than damaged"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"Having no credit history is a different problem from having a bad one, and "
"it is the better problem. There is nothing to argue with and nothing to wait"
" out. You are building on clear ground."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.1.title"
msgid "A secured card is your own money, held"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"You put down a deposit, say 200 dollars, and that becomes your limit. Use a "
"little of it, pay it off every month, and it reports as an ordinary credit "
"card. The deposit comes back. The risk to the bank is nil, which is exactly "
"why they will say yes to somebody with no history."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.2.title"
msgid "A builder loan runs backwards"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"The bank holds the money in an account, you make payments, and you get the "
"money at the end. You are not borrowing anything. What you are buying is 12 "
"months of on-time payment history, which is the single heaviest thing in the"
" formula."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.3.title"
msgid "The cheapest route is somebody else's card"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"Being added as an authorized user on a family member's long-standing card "
"can put their history on your file without you ever touching the card. It "
"costs nothing and takes one phone call from them. Ask somebody who has had "
"the same card a long time and always paid it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.3.aside"
msgid "It works both ways, so only ask somebody whose own record is solid."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.4.title"
msgid "Rent, phone and power can count"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.card.4.body"
msgid ""
"Payments you are already making can be reported, through services set up for"
" it. It is the least work for the biggest effect, because you are getting "
"credit for money that was leaving your pocket anyway."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"You have no credit file and 200 dollars. What starts the clock fastest?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.check.why"
msgid ""
"The 200 becomes your limit and the account starts reporting straight away. "
"Applying for regular credit with no file mostly produces refusals, and each "
"one leaves a mark. Waiting costs you the one thing you cannot buy later, "
"which is time on the account. Getting added as an authorized user on "
"somebody else's card costs nothing at all and can run alongside it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.check.choice.secured"
msgid "A secured card, used lightly and paid in full monthly"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.check.choice.wait"
msgid "Wait until you have more money saved"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.building-from-nothing.check.choice.loan"
msgid "Apply for a regular loan and see what happens"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.title"
msgid "If somebody has been using your name"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.hook"
msgid ""
"It happens more to people inside than to anybody else, and the tools to stop"
" it are free."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.card.0.title"
msgid "Why this hits this population hardest"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"Your Social Security number has been on paperwork in a lot of hands. You "
"have not seen a statement in years. Mail goes to an address that is not "
"yours. Accounts opened in your name can run for a long time before anybody "
"who cares finds out. If your report shows accounts you have never heard of, "
"you are not confused, and it is not your fault."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.card.1.title"
msgid "A freeze is free and it is the strong one"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"A security freeze stops anybody opening new credit in your name. It has to "
"be placed free of charge, within one business day of an electronic or phone "
"request and three business days of a mailed one. Lifting it when you "
"actually want credit is free too, within an hour if you do it "
"electronically."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.card.2.title"
msgid "A fraud alert is the lighter version"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"An initial alert lasts at least a year and comes with a free copy of your "
"file. File an identity theft report and you can get an extended alert: seven"
" years, two free copies in the first year, and your name kept off "
"unsolicited credit offers for five."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.card.3.title"
msgid "An account you never opened is a dispute, not a debt"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"Do not pay it and do not negotiate it. It goes down the dispute route, and "
"unverifiable items have to be removed. Tell your coordinator which items you"
" do not recognize. That sentence is the one that starts the legal clock."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"Your report shows a card opened two years ago that you have never heard of. "
"What is the first move?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.check.why"
msgid ""
"Saying you do not recognize it is what turns this into a dispute, and a "
"dispute puts the bureau on a 30-day clock. Paying it can be read as agreeing"
" it is yours. Waiting seven years means seven years of it sitting on your "
"file while you are trying to rent somewhere. A freeze on top of that stops "
"the next one."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.check.choice.dispute"
msgid "Tell your coordinator you do not recognize it"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.check.choice.pay"
msgid "Pay it off so it stops growing"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.identity-theft.check.choice.ignore"
msgid "Ignore it, it will age off in seven years"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.title"
msgid "Spotting the people who will take your money"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.hook"
msgid ""
"Coming home with a bit of money and a bad report makes you a target. Two "
"rules cover most of it."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.scams.card.0.title"
msgid "Rule one: nobody may charge you before the work is done"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.scams.card.0.body"
msgid ""
"A credit repair company cannot legally take any money before it has fully "
"performed what it promised. Not a deposit, not a setup fee, not a first "
"month. If money is wanted up front, the law has already been broken and you "
"have learned everything you need to know about them."
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.scams.card.1.title"
msgid ""
"Rule two: anybody telling you to change your identity is setting you up"
msgstr ""

#. LEGAL: cites a statute, read this one twice.
msgctxt "lesson.scams.card.1.body"
msgid ""
"Advising you to alter your identifying information to hide a bad record is "
"specifically prohibited, and the person doing it is walking you into a fraud"
" charge while they keep the fee. The same goes for anyone telling you to "
"misstate your history."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.card.2.title"
msgid "There is nothing they can do that you cannot"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.card.2.body"
msgid ""
"Every dispute a paid company files is one you can file yourself, free, in a "
"letter. There is no special channel and no relationship with the bureaus. "
"What they are selling is the letter you are already getting help with here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.card.3.title"
msgid "Accurate is accurate"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.card.3.body"
msgid ""
"If a debt is genuinely yours and correctly reported, nobody can remove it "
"early. Anybody promising to delete accurate information is either lying or "
"planning to dispute things they know are true, which wastes your time and "
"can get the disputes dismissed as frivolous."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.check.prompt"
msgid ""
"A company offers to fix your credit for 99 dollars a month starting now. "
"What does that tell you?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.check.why"
msgid ""
"Taking money before the service is fully performed is prohibited outright. "
"You do not need to read a single review: the payment structure alone tells "
"you what they are. And the disputes they would file are ones you can file "
"yourself for the price of a stamp."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.check.choice.illegal"
msgid "They are already breaking the law by charging before the work"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.check.choice.fair"
msgid "It is a fair price if it works"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "lesson.scams.check.choice.check"
msgid "Nothing yet, check their reviews first"
msgstr ""
